host macOS clone (Mac hand) -- Eastern (EDT) one-clock
title the second mitra shed -- ten elders cut, and the eight witnesses that were guarding them
prompt Keaton circled a mitra shed of all that has been prepped, all loops stopped, the trees to be updated together after.
think Checkpoint 20260827.162143 (walk-back 5707335d0f) went down before anything moved, then a thirteen-agent sweep read every prepped fossil against the whole tree. It paid for itself twice. First: EIGHT chapter witnesses assert these fossils EXIST on disk -- they were written to prove a molt by testing that the elder sat there carrying its banner, which is a proof that cannot survive the cut it was preparing for. Second, and sharper: FOUR of the eight were ALREADY RED before the shed touched a byte, and all four trace to one root -- oven/ became ember/ on 20260808, the bake seat became Kiln on 20260827, ASCII-first swept the middots, and the chapter witnesses were unrostered so nothing reached them. Booked as REDS %292 and repaired in the same round; a fifth stale leg surfaced mid-proof, a witness pinned to the Oven Chapter reading OPEN when prin_scope had carried it to PAUSED.
think The eight moved to the stronger reading: the elder is GONE, and the prep pin's shed-complete record names it. Ten elders cut -- six June and p31 foundations, the Oven bake-seat page its Kiln mutant replaced, the anvil-to-oven naming counsel the LEXICON's Ember row carries, the swarm-that-feeds elder, the six-chapter double-seat whose eight-chapter mutant accretes all six whole. Nineteen living citers repointed first across four disjoint agent groups; each cut basename seated as a LISTED deliberate absence so the census reads intent rather than breakage; a dead template-manifest exclusion row retired.
think THREE were walked and HELD as Class W3 rather than cut, and the measurement is why. The oct charter's named mutant is the LEXICON's Ember row, which carries the naming and not the chapter's seat table -- three witnesses grep that table and prin_scope prints its path, so cutting it would break working guards to tidy one file. The three-stars charter holds the naming derivation SIX times against the living charter's ONE reference: an elder whose mutant cites rather than retells is not superseded. The planets charter was ninety minutes old and is the middle link of a provenance chain a versioned recursion prompt still reads.
obs The foundations_link guard caught my own classifier error before it shipped, and its own why explains it: in foundations/ a stamp-named basename is LIVING rather than testimony, because the whole room is stamp-named -- the generic dated test is right for a session log and wrong for that room. Five links repointed there; links_broken back to 0 of 480.
obs Proven on metal after the cut: all eight chapter witnesses GREEN, foundations_link 0 of 480, dated_path, tracked_link, living_docs_lint, living_card_ascii, alias_sameness 13 checks 0 faults, skate_native_core, and both REDS guards. Pins under bound -- SHRED_PREP 24,676 and REDS 20,874.
loom shed_cut=10 shed_held=3 witnesses_molted=8 witnesses_pre_red=4 living_repointed=19 listed_absences=34 reds_row=292 foundations_links=480
file construction/SHRED_PREP.md Class H becomes the shed-complete record; Class W3 seats the three held
